{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem he became Count of Tripoli after his father's death in 1152. He was a member of the House of Toulouse and played a significant role in the history of the Crusader states. \n*Early Life and Reign* \nRaymond III was born around 1140 and was the son of Raymond II and Hodierna he was still a minor when his father died and his mother acted as regent until he came of age. He became Count of Tripoli in 1152 and was known for his military campaigns against the Muslim states. \n*Relationship with the Kingdom of Jerusalem* \nRaymond III had a complex relationship with the Kingdom of Jerusalem he was a vassal of the king but also sought to maintain his independence. He married Hodierna's niece but the marriage was childless and he later married a woman named Alice but this marriage was also childless. \n*Military Campaigns and Death* \nRaymond III led several military campaigns against the Muslim states including the Battle of Inab in 1149 and the Battle of Montgisard in 1177. He was taken prisoner by Saladin in 1164 but was released after a ransom was paid. He died in 1187 without an heir and the county of Tripoli was inherited by his nephew Raymond IV. \n*Legacy and Succession* \nRaymond III played a significant role in the history of the Crusader states and was known for his military campaigns and his complex relationship with the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He was the last count of Tripoli from the House of Toulouse and his death marked the end of an era. \n*Capture and Imprisonment* \nRaymond III was captured by Saladin in 1164 and was imprisoned for several years. He was released after a ransom was paid and returned to Tripoli where he continued to rule until his death. \n*Battle of Hattin* \nRaymond III did not participate in the Battle of Hattin in 1187 where the Crusader army was defeated by Saladin. He died shortly after the battle without an heir and the county of Tripoli was inherited by his nephew Raymond IV.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -9.775113539944869e-06}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0004884004010818899}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.0002907091984525323}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.4858165979385376}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.3212256133556366}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -2.145764938177308e-06}, {"token": " II", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.02842830866575241}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -6.12716976320371e-05}, {"token": " H", "logprob": -0.0010705222375690937}, {"token": "odi", "logprob": -0.001495434669777751}, {"token": "erna", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Jerusalem", "logprob": -0.000644237850792706}, {"token": " he", "logprob": -0.03839263319969177}, {"token": " became", "logprob": -1.2496232986450195}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.8571782112121582}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -2.3841830625315197e-06}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " after", "logprob": -1.205370306968689}, {"token": " his", "logprob": -0.6931475400924683}, {"token": " father", "logprob": -0.03365003690123558}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -0.03390001505613327}, {"token": " death", "logprob": -0.021694259718060493}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.0018462770385667682}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "115", "logprob": -7.629365427419543e-06}, {"to